 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3. Feature Engineering & Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates feature engineering: creating new features from existing biomarkers and analyzing their relationships with the target variable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup and Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add src to path\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '../')\n",
    "from src.data.loaders import load_processed_data, save_processed_data\n",
    "from src.data.features import FeatureEngineer\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Libraries and modules loaded')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load Processed Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load processed data (normalized)\n",
    "df_processed = pd.read_csv('../data/processed/alzheimers_processed.csv')\n",
    "print(f'Processed data shape: {df_processed.shape}')\nprint(f'\\nColumns: {list(df_processed.columns)}')\nprint(f'\\nFirst few rows:')\nprint(df_processed.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Understanding Original Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Before creating engineered features, let's understand the original biomarkers:\n",
    "- **p_tau**: Phosphorylated tau (phosphorylated form of tau protein)\n",
    "- **np_tau**: Total non-phosphorylated tau\n",
    "- **ab_42**: Amyloid beta-42 (lower in Alzheimer's)\n",
    "- **age**: Patient age\n",
    "- **years_education**: Educational attainment\n",
    "- **mmse**: Mini-Mental State Exam (cognitive score, lower = more impaired)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature Engineering Rationale\n",
    "\n",
    "Domain knowledge suggests:\n",
    "1. **Tau Ratio** (p_tau / total_tau): Proportion of tau that is phosphorylated\n",
    "2. **Biomarker Composite**: Weighted combination of tau and amyloid\n",
    "3. **Cognitive-Age Interaction**: Age modulates cognitive decline\n",
    "4. **Education-Adjusted Cognition**: Education level affects baseline cognition\n",
    "5. **Tau-Amyloid Index**: Ratio of tau to amyloid pathology\n",
    "\n",
    "These features capture biomarker relationships not captured by individual values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load Raw Data for Feature Engineering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load raw data (before normalization) for feature engineering\n",
    "df_raw = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/alzheimers_biomarkers.csv')\n",
    "print(f'Raw data shape: {df_raw.shape}')\nprint(f'\\nBasic statistics:')\nprint(df_raw.describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Initialize Feature Engineer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create feature engineer\nengineers = FeatureEngineer()\nprint('FeatureEngineer initialized')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature 1: Tau Ratio"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create tau ratio: p_tau / (p_tau + np_tau)\ntau_ratio = engineers.create_tau_ratio(df_raw)\n\nprint('Tau Ratio Statistics:')\nprint(f'Mean: {tau_ratio.mean():.4f}')\nprint(f'Std: {tau_ratio.std():.4f}')\nprint(f'Min: {tau_ratio.min():.4f}')\nprint(f'Max: {tau_ratio.max():.4f}')\n\n# Visualize\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\nplt.hist(tau_ratio, bins=30, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7, color='steelblue')\nplt.xlabel('Tau Ratio')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Distribution of Tau Ratio')\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n\n# By target\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\nfor target in [0, 1]:\n    subset = tau_ratio[df_raw['amyloid_positive'] == target]\n    plt.hist(subset, bins=20, alpha=0.6, label=f'Target={target}', edgecolor='black')\nplt.xlabel('Tau Ratio')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Tau Ratio by Amyloid Status')\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature 2: Biomarker Composite"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create biomarker composite: weighted tau and amyloid\nbiomarker_composite = engineers.create_biomarker_composite(df_raw)\n\nprint('Biomarker Composite Statistics:')\nprint(f'Mean: {biomarker_composite.mean():.4f}')\nprint(f'Std: {biomarker_composite.std():.4f}')\nprint(f'Min: {biomarker_composite.min():.4f}')\nprint(f'Max: {biomarker_composite.max():.4f}')\n\n# Visualize\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\nplt.hist(biomarker_composite, bins=30, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7, color='coral')\nplt.xlabel('Biomarker Composite')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Distribution of Biomarker Composite')\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n\n# By target\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\nfor target in [0, 1]:\n    subset = biomarker_composite[df_raw['amyloid_positive'] == target]\n    plt.hist(subset, bins=20, alpha=0.6, label=f'Target={target}', edgecolor='black')\nplt.xlabel('Biomarker Composite')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Biomarker Composite by Amyloid Status')\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature 3: Cognitive-Age Interaction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create cognitive-age interaction: age × cognitive decline\ncog_age_interaction = engineers.create_cognitive_age_interaction(df_raw)\n\nprint('Cognitive-Age Interaction Statistics:')\nprint(f'Mean: {cog_age_interaction.mean():.4f}')\nprint(f'Std: {cog_age_interaction.std():.4f}')\nprint(f'Min: {cog_age_interaction.min():.4f}')\nprint(f'Max: {cog_age_interaction.max():.4f}')\n\n# Visualize\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\nplt.hist(cog_age_interaction, bins=30, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7, color='lightgreen')\nplt.xlabel('Cognitive-Age Interaction')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Distribution of Cognitive-Age Interaction')\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n\n# By target\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\nfor target in [0, 1]:\n    subset = cog_age_interaction[df_raw['amyloid_positive'] == target]\n    plt.hist(subset, bins=20, alpha=0.6, label=f'Target={target}', edgecolor='black')\nplt.xlabel('Cognitive-Age Interaction')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Cognitive-Age Interaction by Amyloid Status')\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature 4: Education-Adjusted Cognition"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create education-adjusted cognition: mmse / years_education\nedu_adj_cognition = engineers.create_education_adjusted_cognition(df_raw)\n\nprint('Education-Adjusted Cognition Statistics:')\nprint(f'Mean: {edu_adj_cognition.mean():.4f}')\nprint(f'Std: {edu_adj_cognition.std():.4f}')\nprint(f'Min: {edu_adj_cognition.min():.4f}')\nprint(f'Max: {edu_adj_cognition.max():.4f}')\n\n# Visualize\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\nplt.hist(edu_adj_cognition, bins=30, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7, color='skyblue')\nplt.xlabel('Education-Adjusted Cognition')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Distribution of Education-Adjusted Cognition')\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n\n# By target\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\nfor target in [0, 1]:\n    subset = edu_adj_cognition[df_raw['amyloid_positive'] == target]\n    plt.hist(subset, bins=20, alpha=0.6, label=f'Target={target}', edgecolor='black')\nplt.xlabel('Education-Adjusted Cognition')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Education-Adjusted Cognition by Amyloid Status')\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature 5: Tau-Amyloid Index"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create tau-amyloid index: p_tau / ab_42\ntau_amyloid_index = engineers.create_tau_amyloid_index(df_raw)\n\nprint('Tau-Amyloid Index Statistics:')\nprint(f'Mean: {tau_amyloid_index.mean():.4f}')\nprint(f'Std: {tau_amyloid_index.std():.4f}')\nprint(f'Min: {tau_amyloid_index.min():.4f}')\nprint(f'Max: {tau_amyloid_index.max():.4f}')\n\n# Visualize\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\nplt.hist(tau_amyloid_index, bins=30, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7, color='plum')\nplt.xlabel('Tau-Amyloid Index')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Distribution of Tau-Amyloid Index')\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n\n# By target\nplt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\nfor target in [0, 1]:\n    subset = tau_amyloid_index[df_raw['amyloid_positive'] == target]\n    plt.hist(subset, bins=20, alpha=0.6, label=f'Target={target}', edgecolor='black')\nplt.xlabel('Tau-Amyloid Index')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.title('Tau-Amyloid Index by Amyloid Status')\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Apply Full Feature Engineering Pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Apply complete feature engineering\ndf_engineered = engineers.engineer_features(df_raw)\n\nprint(f'Original features: {df_raw.shape[1]}')\nprint(f'Engineered features: {df_engineered.shape[1]}')\nprint(f'\\nNew shape: {df_engineered.shape}')\nprint(f'\\nColumn names:')\nprint(list(df_engineered.columns))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Engineered Features Summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Show statistics of engineered features\nengineered_cols = ['tau_ratio', 'biomarker_composite', 'cog_age_interaction', 'edu_adj_cognition', 'tau_amyloid_index']\n\nprint('Engineered Features Statistics:')\nprint(df_engineered[engineered_cols].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Correlation Analysis: All Features"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compute correlation matrix\ncorr_matrix = df_engineered.corr()\n\n# Plot correlation heatmap\nplt.figure(figsize=(14, 10))\nsns.heatmap(corr_matrix, annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='coolwarm', center=0, \n            square=True, linewidths=0.5, cbar_kws={\"shrink\": 0.8})\nplt.title('Correlation Matrix: Original + Engineered Features')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n# Correlations with target\nprint('\\nFeature Correlations with Target (amyloid_positive):')\nprint('-' * 60)\ntarget_corr = corr_matrix['amyloid_positive'].sort_values(ascending=False)\nfor feature, corr_val in target_corr.items():\n    print(f'{feature:30} | {corr_val:7.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature Importance Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Feature importance based on target correlation\nprint('Feature Importance (|correlation with target|):')\nprint('-' * 60)\nabs_corr = corr_matrix['amyloid_positive'].abs().sort_values(ascending=False)\nfor feature, abs_corr_val in abs_corr.items():\n    if feature != 'amyloid_positive':\n        print(f'{feature:30} | {abs_corr_val:7.4f}')\n\n# Visualize feature importance\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 8))\nabs_corr_plot = abs_corr[abs_corr.index != 'amyloid_positive']\ncolors = ['#2ecc71' if x > 0.3 else '#3498db' for x in abs_corr_plot.values]\nabs_corr_plot.plot(kind='barh', color=colors, edgecolor='black', ax=ax)\nax.set_xlabel('|Correlation with Target|')\nax.set_title('Feature Importance: Correlation Analysis')\nax.grid(axis='x', alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Original vs Engineered Feature Comparison"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compare original and engineered features\noriginal_features = ['p_tau', 'np_tau', 'ab_42', 'age', 'years_education', 'mmse']\nengineered_features = ['tau_ratio', 'biomarker_composite', 'cog_age_interaction', 'edu_adj_cognition', 'tau_amyloid_index']\n\nprint('ORIGINAL FEATURES - Correlation with Target')\nprint('-' * 50)\nfor feat in original_features:\n    corr = corr_matrix.loc[feat, 'amyloid_positive']\n    print(f'{feat:20} | {corr:7.4f}')\n\nprint('\\nENGINEERED FEATURES - Correlation with Target')\nprint('-' * 50)\nfor feat in engineered_features:\n    corr = corr_matrix.loc[feat, 'amyloid_positive']\n    print(f'{feat:30} | {corr:7.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Normalize Engineered Features"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code">
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Normalize engineered features for model training\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n\nX = df_engineered.drop('amyloid_positive', axis=1)\ny = df_engineered['amyloid_positive']\n\nscaler = StandardScaler()\nX_normalized = scaler.fit_transform(X)\ndf_engineered_normalized = pd.DataFrame(X_normalized, columns=X.columns)\ndf_engineered_normalized['amyloid_positive'] = y.values\n\nprint(f'Engineered features (normalized) shape: {df_engineered_normalized.shape}')\nprint(f'\\nFirst few rows:')\nprint(df_engineered_normalized.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Save Engineered Features"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Save engineered features\noutput_path = '../data/processed/alzheimers_engineered.csv'\ndf_engineered_normalized.to_csv(output_path, index=False)\n\nprint(f'Engineered features saved to: {output_path}')\n\n# Verify\ndf_verify = pd.read_csv(output_path)\nprint(f'Verification - shape: {df_verify.shape}')\nprint(f'Verification - columns: {list(df_verify.columns)}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary of Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "### Engineered Features Created:\n",
    "1. **tau_ratio**: Proportion of phosphorylated tau (domain-informed)\n",
    "2. **biomarker_composite**: Weighted tau and amyloid combination\n",
    "3. **cog_age_interaction**: Age-modulated cognitive decline\n",
    "4. **edu_adj_cognition**: Education-adjusted cognitive score\n",
    "5. **tau_amyloid_index**: Tau pathology relative to amyloid\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Insights:\n",
    "- Engineered features capture biomarker relationships\n",
    "- Feature correlations reveal predictive signals\n",
    "- Domain knowledge informs feature creation\n",
    "- Normalized features are ready for model training\n",
    "- All 12 features (7 original + 5 engineered) saved to `alzheimers_engineered.csv`"
   ]
  }
 ],
